 "result": "Based on the subagent's report, two tests fail for reasons independent of the `partitioned` cookie problem:\n\n1. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**: `src/tessel/app.py:1096` (`ensure_sync`) raises `RuntimeError` because Tessel's `async` extra (probably asgiref) isn't installed. This is a missing optional dependency, unrelated to Werkzeug's cookie handling.\n\n2. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**: `Request.max_form_memory_size` is `None` instead of 500000. The subagent attributed this to Werkzeug 3.0.3 lacking that setting, which arrived in 3.1. That makes it the same *package* problem but a different *code path* from the `partitioned` kwarg. The Tessel line that applies the setting wasn't traced, so this attribution is a likely inference, not a confirmed one.\n\nA third test, `test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`, failed only in the first run and passed on re-run. The subagent believes it was a side effect of a generator leaked by the failed streaming test, so it is indirectly tied to the main cause, not independent.",
